# Findings in git history that are known, reviewed, and kept, per ADR-0202.
#
# An entry hides one finding at one commit, by fingerprint. It is not a path allowlist: a new secret in the same file still fails.
# Every entry states the reason and the rotation decision next to it.
#
# The fix for a committed secret is rotation, not deletion. A revert leaves the value in the history of every clone.
# So each entry records what happened to the credential, not only that it is old.

